## Why This Is Asked
This angle tests practical edge compute handling: budget-aware routing, deterministic fallbacks, and testability in real apps.

## Key Concepts
- Budget-aware orchestration: enforce per-request time budgets for compute paths
- Deterministic fallback: seed heuristic with user_id_masked and client_timestamp for reproducibility
- Telemetry: track latency, fallback usage, and model_version for auditing
- Testability: budget-bound tests, fairness across devices, end-to-end reproducibility

## Code Example
```javascript
function selectScore(input){
  const {budgetMs, start}=input;
  const canRunModel = simulateModelCost(input) <= budgetMs;
  if(!canRunModel){
    return heuristicScore(input.user_id_masked, input.client_timestamp);
  }
  return modelScore(input);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you ensure reproducibility if the heuristic depends on timestamps with clock drift?
- How would you expand this to multi-tenant environments with fair queueing?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes ability to design a real-time, privacy-preserving streaming system with strict latency, security, and auditability requirements. It tests how a candidate handles continuous data ingestion, secure aggregation in a streaming window, dynamic key rotation, and robust testing under adversarial conditions.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time streaming with windowed aggregation
- Online differential privacy and secure aggregation
- Key rotation and attestation for TEEs
- Replay protection and auditable provenance
- Burst handling, clock skew, and fault tolerance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lightweight sketch of stream_submit handler
function handleStreamSubmit(req, res) {
  const { device_id, region, ts, window_id, score_share, signature } = req.body;
  // verify signature, map to window, apply masking
  res.status(202).send({ accepted: true, window_id });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you enforce per-window privacy budgets across tenants and handle overages?
- How would late-arriving shares affect the current window and what reprocessing strategy would you adopt?

